---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import Connections from '../components/Connections.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import {current,groups} from '../lib/connections';
import Code from '../components/Code.astro';
import WorksWith from '../components/WorksWith.astro';
import {githubUrl,defaultBranch} from '../lib/links.mjs';
import snippets from '../../../../docs/onboarding/snippets.json';
const worker='https://slurp.YOUR-SUBDOMAIN.workers.dev';
const fill=(t:string)=>t.replaceAll('YOUR_INGEST_URL',worker+'/v1/events').replaceAll('YOUR_ORIGIN',worker).replaceAll('YOUR_HOST',worker.replace('https://','')).replaceAll('YOUR_PROJECT_ID','prj_…').replaceAll('YOUR_PUBLISHABLE_KEY','slurp_pk_…');
const recipes=[['JavaScript and TypeScript','npm install @hitslop/slurp-sdk','sdk'],['React Native and Expo','npm install @hitslop/slurp-react-native @react-native-async-storage/async-storage','reactNative'],['Swift','Xcode: File → Add Package Dependencies → https://github.com/hitSlop/slurp','swift'],['Segment SDKs','Keep your SDK; your publishable key is the write key','segment'],['Sentry SDKs','Keep your SDK; change the DSN','sentry']] as const;
const sections=[{id:'sdks',label:'Install an SDK'},{id:'today',label:'Works today'},{id:'roadmap',label:'Exploring'},{id:'jev',label:'Jev'}];
---
<Page title="Connections" description="Current Slurp SDK, HTTP, and agent workflows, plus ideas being explored for future connections." current="connections" sections={sections}>
<header class="connections-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Connections</p><h1>Your app. Your tools.<br/><span class="hot">Your agent.</span></h1><p class="lede">Bring events home and work with them locally. Here’s what works today, and where we could take it next.</p></header>
<section id="sdks" class="section"><span class="section-number">01 / SDKS</span><h2>Install an SDK, or keep the one you have.</h2><p>Every path lands in the same archive and the same DuckDB table. <code>slurp init</code> creates your project and its first publishable key and prints that key with your ingest URL; the examples below show where each one goes.</p><WorksWith/><p class="notice">JavaScript is published. React Native and Swift are in preview: tested against fakes and a local Worker, not yet run on a device. Segment and Sentry SDKs are verified with analytics-node, analytics-next, analytics-swift, @sentry/node and @sentry/browser; other Segment and Sentry SDKs should work the same way but are untested. Coming, with no dates: Python, Rust and Kotlin SDKs, and local symbolication of Sentry stack traces. Logos are trademarks of their owners and are used only to show compatibility.</p>{recipes.map(([title,how,key])=><div class="recipe"><h3>{title}</h3><p class="fine">{how}</p><Code label="Example" code={fill(snippets[key])}/></div>)}<p><a href={`${githubUrl}/blob/${defaultBranch}/docs/sdks.md`}>Every option, mapping and limit ↗</a></p></section>
<section id="today" class="section"><span class="section-number">02 / WORKS TODAY</span><h2>Start with your app and your agent.</h2><p>Capture with an SDK, your existing Segment or Sentry SDK, or the HTTP API. New events are sealed into archives about every 10 minutes; sync them with the CLI, then let your agent query the local data. Agent entries describe CLI workflows.</p><Connections items={current}/></section>
<section id="roadmap" class="section"><span class="section-number">03 / EXPLORING</span><h2>More of your stack, together.</h2><p class="notice">These connections are ideas being explored. They are not available to connect, and have no announced release dates.</p>{groups.map(g=><section class="connection-group" id={g.id}><h3>{g.title}</h3><Connections items={g.items}/></section>)}</section>
<section id="jev" class="section"><span class="section-number">04 / JEV · EXPLORING</span><h2>Something that notices.</h2><p>Jev is an idea for classifying incoming events and routing useful signals to an agent. This workflow is illustrative; processing and alert delivery are not available.</p><div class="steps"><div><Icon name="connections"/><h3>Events arrive</h3><p>From your app and future connections.</p></div><div><Icon name="agent"/><h3>Jev classifies</h3><p>Identify a possible signal and its confidence.</p></div><div><Icon name="webhook"/><h3>Alerts go out</h3><p>Hand the evidence to an agent or endpoint.</p></div></div><p class="fine">Illustrative signals: a spike in export failures, a new error pattern, stalled onboarding, or possible churn.</p><a class="btn" href="/docs/">Get started with what works today ↗</a></section>
</Page>
